WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.969 --> 00:00:04.310
Phoebe Cates was one of the biggest teen stars
of the 1980s.

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:08.010
After making her big-screen debut in the Blue
Lagoon knockoff Paradise, she starred in a

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:12.390
string of quintessential '80s movies, including
Fast Times at Ridgemont High, Private School,

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:13.390
and Gremlins.

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:18.289
It looked like Cates was here to stay—until
the mid-1990s, when she just kind of…vanished.

00:00:18.289 --> 00:00:21.529
Here are the real reasons Phoebe Cates disappeared
from Hollywood.

00:00:21.529 --> 00:00:22.529
Motherhood

00:00:22.529 --> 00:00:26.210
Shortly after her breakthrough role in Fast
Times at Ridgemont High, Cates auditioned

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:30.339
for more adult roles, including Chloe in the
Baby Boomer classic The Big Chill.

00:00:30.339 --> 00:00:34.260
She didn't get the part—it went to Meg Tilly—but
she got to meet one of the film's stars, Kevin

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.260
Kline.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:39.160
They married in 1989 and now have two children
together, a son named Owen and a daughter,

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:40.160
Greta.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:43.040
Like a lot of parents, Cates decided that
she preferred focusing on raising a family

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:46.050
to pursuing a full-time career outside the
home.

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:47.280
String Of Bad Luck

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.990
The movies Cates starred in toward the end
of her working years weren't exactly blockbusters

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:51.990
anyway.

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:55.980
Despite being the long-awaited sequel to a
very popular movie, Gremlins 2: The New Batch

00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:00.000
took in a relatively disappointing $41 million
in 1990.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.470
Drop Dead Fred made $13 million when it arrived
in theaters the following year, and her final

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:09.860
major film, the quirky 1994 comedy Princess
Caraboo, earned just $2.9 million during a

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.100
disappointing theatrical run.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.280
Lack Of Interest

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:16.670
Even though she was focused on being a mom,
Cates didn't completely retire.

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:21.300
Her last major role was in the 2001 independent
movie The Anniversary Party.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:25.110
She took the part as a favor to the director,
Jennifer Jason Leigh, one of her best friends

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:27.909
since the two played pals in Fast Times at
Ridgemont High.

00:01:27.909 --> 00:01:31.409
That role is one of a small handful of projects
that Cates has deemed worthy of leaving her

00:01:31.409 --> 00:01:33.729
kids at home to pursue.

00:01:33.729 --> 00:01:34.729
Charity Work

00:01:34.729 --> 00:01:37.510
Cates' son Owen has juvenile diabetes.

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:41.531
Since seeing its effects firsthand, Cates
and Kline devote a lot of time, effort, and

00:01:41.531 --> 00:01:45.030
money toward fundraising efforts to find a
cure for the metabolic disease.

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:49.310
Among the organizations Cates supports is
the Juvenile Diabetes Research Foundation,

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:53.780
which puts on benefits like Rock the Cure
and the Promise Ball to raise money for research.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.170
A New Calling

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:58.799
Cates lives in Manhattan's fancy Upper East
Side, which is also where she operates an

00:01:58.799 --> 00:02:01.260
upscale boutique called Blue Tree.

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:05.430
The store started off selling expensive designer
toys, but has expanded to include clothing,

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:06.979
housewares, and specialty foods.

00:02:06.979 --> 00:02:09.259
She told USA Today in 2006:

00:02:09.259 --> 00:02:11.060
"I always wanted to have a general store.

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:14.250
If I could have had a photo booth and sold
candy, I would have."

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:17.950
Clearly Cates is open to the idea of selling
all kinds of things at Blue Tree.

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:19.450
So would she sell a mogwai, then?

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:21.130
"I'll give you $200.

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:23.150
That's $200!"

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:27.030
"I'm sorry, mogwai, not for sale."

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:28.040
Ah, well.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:30.140
Probably better off.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:34.720
Thanks for watching!

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:38.100
